      "item_body": "<p>[A]</p><p>The squirrel population in a small self-contained forest was studied by a biologist. The biologist found that the squirrel population, P, measured in hundreds, is a function of time, t, where t is measured in weeks. The function is P(t) = 20/(1 + 3e^(-0.02t)).</p><p>a. Determine the population at the start of the study, when t = 0.</p><p>b. The largest population the forest can sustain is represented mathematically by the limit as t -&gt; infinity. Determine this limit.</p><p>c. Determine the point of inflection.</p><p>d. Graph the function.</p><p>e. Explain the meaning of the point of inflection in terms of squirrel population growth.</p>",
      "user_response_type": "Text",
      "interaction_type": {
        "name": "Essay",
        "slug": "essay",
        "id": "9"
      },
      "outcome_alignment_set_guid": null,
      "id": "63388",
      "label": null,
      "title": "Q3 [A]",
      "properties": {
